won  if she was losing she would often storm  off more than once she ran directly  through a screen on the door  during high school she developed her  work ethic often staying up late to  study she quickly became a straight a  student and even started her own  business  she sold c plus plus compilers a type of  software that translates computer code  to chinese schools  she started taking mandarin lessons and  partway through high school talked her  way into being accepted by stanford  university's summer program which  culminated in a trip to beijing  inspired by her great great grandfather  christian holmes a surgeon she decided  she wanted to go into medicine but she  discovered early on that she was  terrified of needles  that was what led her to start her own  company  theranos  she went to stanford to study chemical  engineering when she was a freshman she  became a president scholar an honor  which came with a three thousand dollar  stipend to go toward a research project  she spent the summer after her freshman  year interning at the genome institute  in singapore she got the job partly  because she spoke mandarin  as a sophomore she went to one of her  professors and asked to start a company  with his blessing she founded real-time  cures  later changing the company's name to  theranos  thanks to a typo early employees  paychecks actually said real-time curses  she soon filed a patent application for  a medical device for chemical monitoring  and drug delivery a wearable device that  would administer medication monitor  patients blood and adjust the dosage as  needed  by the next semester she had dropped out  of stanford altogether and was working  on theranos in the basement of a college  house  her invention was the edison here's how  it worked  a pin prick would take a tiny sample of  blood from the patient's finger and kept  in a nanotainer the nanotainer would  then be inserted into the edison machine  for analysis and produce rapid results  for 130 tests  theranosis business model was based  around the idea that it could run blood  tests using proprietary technology that  required only a finger pinprick and a  small amount of blood  she said the tests would be able to  detect medical conditions like cancer  and high cholesterol  she started raising money for theranos  from prominent investors like oracle  founder larry ellison and tim draper  theronus raised more than 700 million  dollars she took investors money on the  condition that she wouldn't have to  reveal how theronos technology worked  plus she would have final say over  everything having to do with the company  that obsession with secrecy extended to  every aspect of theranos  for the first decade she spent building  her company theranos operated in stealth  mode  she even took three former theronis  employees to court claiming that he had  misused theranos trade secrets  her attitude towards secrecy and running  a company was borrowed from a silicon  valley hero of hers  former apple ceo steve jobs  she started dressing in black  turtlenecks like jobs decorated her  office with his favorite furniture and  like jobs never took vacations  she also put on a deep voice which may  have been part of a carefully crafted  image intended to help her fit into the  male dominated business world  she was a demanding boss and wanted her  employees to work as hard as she did  she had assistance track when employees  arrived and left each day to encourage  people to work longer hours she started  having dinner catered to the office  around 8 pm each night  shortly after she dropped out of  stanford at age 19 she began dating  theranos president and ceo sunny balwani  who was 20 years older than her  the two met during her third year in  stanford's summer mandarin program the  summer before she went to college  she was bullied by some of the other  students and barwani had come to her aid  barwani became her number two at  theranos despite having little  experience 